  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/48DC2F">Definition <span data-tag="48DC2F">5.5.8.8</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a small $\infty $-category which admits finite coproducts. We let $\calP _{\Sigma }(\calC )$ denote the full subcategory of $\calP (\calC )$ spanned by those functors $\calC ^{op} \rightarrow \SSet $ which preserve finite products. </p>
